                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rodzaj dalmatyki noszonej przez arcykapłanów w starożytnym Izraelu"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1d80502-4b7e-4ea7-9639-0e822f624d4b",
                                "sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                                "text": "Kapłan Matatiasz wdział efod i powoli ruszył w stronę ołtarza."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "58d75990-76dd-459a-ab21-7e7cf3c1cd2a",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "ephod",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ephod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b304494-564b-3b33-92d0-4ed7ebfc72d4",
                                        "entry_id": "58b9fd58-1189-323b-854d-ce16d26228ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A priestly apron, or breastplate, described in the Bible in Exodus 28: vi–xxx, which only the chief priest of ancient Israel was allowed to wear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judaism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "895262f3-a610-49a6-98f7-cb771f70750b",
                                                "sense_id": "0b304494-564b-3b33-92d0-4ed7ebfc72d4",
                                                "text": "1769, Oxford Standard text, Bible (King James): Exodus, 28, vi-viii,\nAnd they shall make the ephod of gold, of blue, and of purple, of scarlet, and fine twined linen, with cunning work.\nIt shall have the two shoulderpieces thereof joined at the two edges thereof; and so it shall be joined together.\nAnd the curious girdle of the ephod, which is upon it, shall be of the same, according to the work thereof; even of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6fa1a5e-7a7b-41e2-af56-787c809f0781",
                                                "sense_id": "0b304494-564b-3b33-92d0-4ed7ebfc72d4",
                                                "text": "1769, Oxford Standard text, Bible (King James): Hosea, 3, iv,\nFor the children of Israel shall abide many days without a king, and without a prince, and without a sacrifice, and without an image, and without an ephod, and without teraphim:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4dba0d48-b269-4bdc-bdce-737701b4ad58",
                                                "sense_id": "0b304494-564b-3b33-92d0-4ed7ebfc72d4",
                                                "text": "From this it appears that at least towards the close of the Exile, the Urim and Thummim were considered as something distinct from the ephod of the high priest and the gems with which it was adorned."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d0010044-ceb5-4498-b8f8-228473b3a37e",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "éphod",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "éphod",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adc462ae-b68f-3621-89f3-f8b4a832378b",
                                        "entry_id": "b5141a96-c500-3f13-add3-db44b3b7f4d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vêtement sacerdotal que portaient les prêtres hébreux, décrit dans le livre de l’Exode 28:6 à 30."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3dd01cb0-bea8-40d5-b0bc-ff5afcfea260",
                                                "sense_id": "adc462ae-b68f-3621-89f3-f8b4a832378b",
                                                "text": "Tu feras deux anneaux d’or et tu les mettras sur les deux épaulettes de l'éphod, vers le bas, en avant, près de leur point d’attache au-dessus de l’écharpe de l'éphod."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bae9429a-6456-4f84-bb6d-faf22c9be350",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "efod",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "efod",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b43ef2d-bc28-305a-b8cb-8f22acf3a8d8",
                                        "entry_id": "50784dad-8f99-3d76-bf62-42bdaebc0656",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prenda en forma de túnica o delantal de lino, ceñida por una faja, que formaba parte de las vestiduras rituales de los sacerdotes judíos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcd48e8f-92c8-4a18-a924-a343b5043a46",
                                                "sense_id": "1b43ef2d-bc28-305a-b8cb-8f22acf3a8d8",
                                                "text": "Ca muchos dias estaran los fijos de israel sin rrey & sin capitan & sin sacrifiçio & sin altar & sin efod & sin terafin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd553b30-7cb8-4466-93f4-66052fdb02ab",
                                                "sense_id": "1b43ef2d-bc28-305a-b8cb-8f22acf3a8d8",
                                                "text": "Ya muerto, mi alma siguió el vuelo errático,\nciñendo en Solima, y a Osiris infiel,\nla mitra bicorne y el efod hierático\ndel gran sacerdote del Dios de Israel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ec72887-4bd4-46ec-b828-b1b9c1db6976",
                                                "sense_id": "1b43ef2d-bc28-305a-b8cb-8f22acf3a8d8",
                                                "text": "En Palestina, Poncio Pilato seguía ejerciendo su magistratura de procurador de la misma manera que en los días de Jesús, oscilando siempre entre la debilidad y la brutalidad. Caifás lleva todavía el efod de los pontífices; son los mismos personajes y los mismos odios."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9318f0d9-df14-4f63-9da8-648e3042bb62",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "Efod",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee4000e3-912b-4004-9d6d-d7f8b3353ae9",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "эфод",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "эфод",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b19c5d2c-fa1b-326b-bc8f-1d700f540c8d",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5843b3-8c58-3d10-a35b-49802193ee2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "часть облачения первосвященника, надеваемого при богослужении"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49b0681a-263e-4e76-a24b-ea30e96fdca1",
                                                "sense_id": "b19c5d2c-fa1b-326b-bc8f-1d700f540c8d",
                                                "text": "Когда надевали эфод на плечи, то один конец опускался на переднюю часть тела, и другой — на заднюю, по углам пришивались кисти."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "38a73194-ed3a-4ddc-91dc-95534a2c2f3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7b3e847-0a93-3238-bec4-9338e1f86060",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d725ea4-73af-331e-a6fa-43c8e1d111a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "ефод",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ефод",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71e3ef07-5cfa-37c8-bfd2-2fe8487eea30",
                                        "entry_id": "4654f707-b2e9-3d89-b88d-43c816ece19c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "библейск., истор. в древнем Израиле — часть облачения первосвященника, надеваемого при богослужении"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "373801fa-59bc-4a0e-9837-2403819c4be4",
                                                "sense_id": "71e3ef07-5cfa-37c8-bfd2-2fe8487eea30",
                                                "text": "И привел Моисей Аарона и сынов его и омыл их водою; и возложил на него хитон, и опоясал его поясом, и надел на него верхнюю ризу, и возложил на него ефод, и опоясал его поясом ефода и прикрепил им ефод на нем, и возложил на него наперсник, и на наперсник положил урим и туммим, и возложил на голову его кидар, а на кидар с передней стороны его возложил полированную дощечку, диадиму святыни, как повелел Господь Моисею."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb4013f8-cfb3-4608-9a24-1ed4edb01ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "71e3ef07-5cfa-37c8-bfd2-2fe8487eea30",
                                                "text": "Неясно, покрывал ли ефод спину первосвященника, облегая его тело наподобие жилета, или же располагался только спереди."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
